    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Sell\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for an Underweight posture, which translates to trimming existing exposure. The technical evidence is genuinely weak: AAPL closed at $180.55, below the 10 EMA ($182.11), 50 SMA ($186.74), and marginally below the 200 SMA ($181.30), with a -5.88% 20-day return and negative MACD (-1.65 vs signal -1.23). The plan explicitly states to \"trim 10-20% of the position\" and \"do not initiate new longs at current levels.\" While the fundamentals (strong $39.9B quarterly operating cash flow, $30.6B capital return program) argue against a full exit, the plan's strategic action is to reduce exposure to a modest underweight. The critical downside level is $177.09 (February 2 capitulation low), and a stop-loss just below this protects against a breakdown to the $170s where there is no major support. This is a tactical trim, not a structural exit \u2014 the plan calls for reassessment at the next earnings release or upon a confirmed technical reversal.\n\n**Entry Price**: 180.55\n\n**Stop Loss**: 176.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Trim 10-20% of existing AAPL position to achieve underweight relative to benchmark\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **SELL**",
